# nr-office-e2e-twin: the end-to-end twin of the Office tool (tests/twin_e2e.rs, tests/com_registry.rs of crate mixdog-office) and its recorder

Written without cargo: nothing below has been compiled or run in Rust (rustfmt parsed both test files). The recorder was run once (Node only, against
C:/Project/mixdog with `--tree C:/Project/mixdog`; it launches no browser, no Office, no LibreOffice) and twice more to check the recording repeats:
the two recordings are equal except for the wall times.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/Cargo.toml
Nothing new once the earlier fragments are in. The two test files name: mixdog-core-api, mixdog-fonts, mixdog-fsio, mixdog-js, mixdog-office-author,
mixdog-office-base (dev-dependency with `test-support`, already there), mixdog-office-com, mixdog-office-design, mixdog-office-pdf, mixdog-office-quality,
mixdog-ooxml, mixdog-pdf, mixdog-raster, mixdog-rt (dev-dependency with `test-support`, already there), tokio (`rt`; the test builds its runtime with
`enable_all`, which needs nothing the workspace tokio does not already enable), sha2, tempfile, serde_json. mixdog-core-api is the line nr-office-engine-author-actions.wire adds.

## native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json (the index of the fixture sets)
Add to `sets`, in name order (after "office-dispatch", before "office-engine" if that sorts there); verify with benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/verify-manifests.mjs:

    { "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-e2e.mjs --tree <tree>", "fileCount": 2,
      "manifest": "office-e2e/MANIFEST.json", "manifestSha256": "2d6eddb3a18abf221af57b4ef46c5da818d54236d3953b8a7d1e65e3c511ca28",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-e2e.mjs", "set": "office-e2e", "totalBytes": 338632 }

native/core/fixtures/office-e2e/{scenarios.json,golden.json,MANIFEST.json} and the recorder are in this task's commit (written at their paths, added with
`git add --sparse`). The manifest's `product` block was computed against a scratch git repository (the recorder needs a git checkout under it); its
`refComparison` is therefore meaningless: re-record with `node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-e2e.mjs --tree C:/Project/mixdog` from the
integration tree to get the usual block. The recording's wall times are this machine's.

## compose_flip.rs SERVICE_PENDING
Nothing: no protocol method and no service.

## Results the lead should expect on the first run
The scenarios exist to find differences; the harness lists each one with its scenario and call (`N differences from the recording`). Known to need a look:
- `pdf: begin, qa, render and a finalize...`: Node's render answers `"renderer":"pdfjs"`; whatever the Rust renderer names itself shows as a text difference.
- `data:true` scenario (`docx: a transaction rolled back...`): the data folder's file list is compared, so a file one side writes lazily (the Office COM scripts) shows.
- The Word chart (`add_chart` on a docx) is not in the scenarios: the twin's batch host draws no chart.
